    "sosNote": {"x": 1420, "y": 1560, "w": 440, "maxH": 700, "fill": "orange", "size": "m", "text": "Emergency works in 3 levels — the app picks automatically:\n\n1. Internet (even slow 2G): tiny alert → server → 108 + nearest hospital + family, instantly.\n\n2. No internet, phone signal: one tap opens a ready-made SMS to our gateway number (code + GPS + symptoms), or gives a missed call — caller ID finds the patient.\n\n3. No signal: big Call 112 / 108 (works on any operator's tower). Alert is saved and auto-sends when signal returns. Offline first aid + cached hospital map.\n\nGPS works without network. A web app always needs one tap from the user to send SMS or call.\n\nUse the 'simulate network' switch on screen 7 to see each level."},
    "rwdNote": {"x": 1420, "y": 2320, "w": 440, "maxH": 360, "fill": "teal", "size": "m", "text": "One codebase, 3 layouts:\n• Phone < 640px: bottom tab bar, big SOS card\n• Tablet 640–1024px: side rail + split list / detail\n• Laptop / PC > 1024px: full sidebar, 3-column dashboard\nSOS is always one tap away on every size."}
